    "introduction": "Andreas Pliatsikas moved to NYC from Greece at the age of 21 to study theater and film. He has been featured in several classic stage productions including Suppliants as Adrastus, Caligula as Gaetelicus and Lilies or The Revival Of A Romantic Drama as Bishop Jean Bilodeau. Notable TV/Film credits include Black Rabbit, Privateers, The Christmas Lottery, A Chrismystery and the upcoming comedy feature Bed-Ridden plus Daredevil: Born Again - Season 2. His studies include the National Shakespeare Conservatory (NSC), the American Musical & Dramatic Academy (AMDA), and the HB Studio (HBS). He recently went on to refine his art with some private coaching by Amy Weinstein.",
